You breathe deeply. You have returned to the Temple of Enoa again. Everything
seems to be in best order. The peaceful atmosphere of the buildings makes you
feel comfortable. Especially after your experiences with the Rubyred Aposto-
late you are very happy to be here. You decide to speak with Prior Marcus,
before you take some time for yourself. "Tell me everything", Marcus later
says while you're sitting in his library, having some wonderful black coffee.
"It's strange", you start. "That 'Rubyred Apostolate'...they were both some
kind of rebels against our system, and a religious cult, apparently denying
the five divines. Instead they prayed to Eris, who they call 'the One'. They
were convinced that mankind has to take bloody revenge on the Drekh'Nar. The
leader's plan was to overtake government and then force people join the Apos-
tolate. He wanted to use Northdoom for fighting us. After that, they wanted
to steal our research on the Book of Stars, to somehow get back to the sur-
face and fight the Drekh'Nar. Barfaee said that he knows the true meaning
of the Book of Stars, in contrast to the Temple." You take a big gulp of cof-
fee. Marcus smiles. "I knew you'd solve this case. It's just a pity that
Thanan had to die before we were able to see the threat. I think he was just
used by them." You nod. "Funny thing was...after I killed Astaroth, Barfaee
tried to take Northdoom--but it dissolved to dust. Then Hermes appeared and
spoke to the people. She ordered them to not listen anymore to 'that sorry
old man'. And they did. The Apostolate isn't a danger anymore--they're gone."
